  <p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p>
  <p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;text-decoration:underline;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">Proposal Two &#8211; The Reverse Stock Split Proposal</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;">. The stockholders of the Company approved the proposal to amend the Company&#8217;s Amended and Restated Certificate of Incorporation to effect a reverse stock split of the Company&#8217;s outstanding shares of common stock at a ratio of 1:10 (the &#8220;Reverse Stock Split&#8221;), with the Reverse Stock Split to be effected at such time and date, if at all, as determined by the Board in its sole discretion. The votes were cast as follows:</span></p>
  <p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p>
